 ## Overview
-Image Shrinking reduces the resolution of a volume image when its dimensions exceed the maximum 3D texture size, using trilinear interpolation to preserve data continuity [S2, unofficial]. It differs from [Zero Padding for Aliasing Reduction](6382-zero-padding-for-aliasing-reduction.md) by not explicitly applying a low-pass filter before sampling, and from [3D Pixel Shuffle](19803-3d-pixel-shuffle.md) by using spatial interpolation rather than channel rearrangement. It builds on [3D Image Resize and Crop](2703-3d-image-resize-and-crop.md).
+Image Shrinking reduces the resolution of a volume image by sampling at a lower grid density using trilinear interpolation to preserve data continuity [G]. It differs from [Zero Padding for Aliasing Reduction](6382-zero-padding-for-aliasing-reduction.md) by not explicitly applying a low-pass filter before sampling, and from [3D Pixel Shuffle](19803-3d-pixel-shuffle.md) by using spatial interpolation rather than channel rearrangement [G]. It builds on [3D Image Resize and Crop](2703-3d-image-resize-and-crop.md) [G].
 
