+- **Memory Complexity:** $O(S'_x \times S'_y \times S'_z)$ for the output array [G].
 - **Measured Performance:** Not given in the sources.
-- **Strengths:** Simple to implement; preserves data continuity via interpolation [S2, unofficial]; efficient for moderate downsampling factors.
-- **Limitations:** Does not explicitly filter high frequencies, potentially causing aliasing artifacts if the downsampling factor is large [S2, G, unofficial]; interpolation artifacts (blurring) may occur.
-- **When to use:** When texture size limits are exceeded and a quick, continuous reduction is needed [S2, unofficial].
-- **When not to use:** When aliasing artifacts are unacceptable without pre-filtering [S2, G, unofficial].
